Root cause: v2.1 discovered 52 genres correctly from homepage link analysis,
but threw away the actual href URLs and rebuilt them as /list?genre={id}&period=2
— which returns HTTP 404 for every genre.

v3 fixes:
1. discoverGenres() now captures full href alongside id+name
2. buildGenreUrls(genre) returns multiple candidate URLs:
   - Real href (preferred)
   - /list?genre=N&period=2 (current period)
   - /list?genre=N (no period)
   - /label-ranking?genre=N&period=2 (legacy path)
3. scrapeGenre() tries each URL in turn until one yields labels
4. Body is parsed even on HTTP 404 — Next.js apps often return 404 status
   but still embed __NEXT_DATA__ with the actual data
5. browserHeaders() sends Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate etc. so Cloudflare
   doesn't 404 our fetches
6. Logs first 3 sample hrefs for diagnostic visibility
7. Version banner bumped to v3 so user can verify new code is loaded
